# This .gitignore is conservative because the QNX NCEULA forbids redistributing
# QNX binaries, IFS images, or compiled QNX components in any form. The patterns
# below exist to make accidental commits of QNX-derived artifacts very hard.
#
# KVM here boots our startup-qemu-virt; this is not a QNX-supported
# configuration, and no timing claim attaches to the boot.

# QNX-derived binaries — NEVER commit
*.bin
*.img
*.vmdk
*.iso
**/ifs*.bin
**/disk-qemu.*
output/
# mkqnximage build trees (QNX-derived guest/host artifacts) — NEVER commit.
# Root-anchored so they do NOT also match scripts/qhv/ (committed source).
/qnx-safety-vm/
/qhv/

# QNX SDP install directories
qnx800/
qnx710/

# Model weights stay outside the repository. The manifest records their
# HF repo id, revision, filename and sha256.
*.gguf
*.safetensors
*.onnx
*.pt
*.pth
*.engine
models/
# The 2026-09-18 service's L4T client: source is committed, its build output
# is not (it links TensorRT/CUDA and embeds nothing of ours worth versioning).
ipc-test/compute-client/compute_client
# The VLM service arm's guest monitor (OD13): a qcc-built QNX binary, so never
# committed (NCEULA). Its own name, because every ifs-*.build stages the shared
# ipc-test/qnx-safety-monitor/qnx-safety-monitor, and rebuilding that one would
# change what a later rebuild of ifs-udp/shm/kick embeds. *.bin does not match
# an extensionless binary, which is why each is named here by exact path.
ipc-test/qnx-safety-monitor/qnx-safety-monitor-svc
# The liveness deadline's guest monitor (OD14), for the same reasons.
ipc-test/qnx-safety-monitor/qnx-safety-monitor-live
# Guest-side timestamps' guest monitor (OD15), for the same reasons.
ipc-test/qnx-safety-monitor/qnx-safety-monitor-stamp
ipc-test/qnx-safety-monitor/qnx-safety-monitor-bell
ipc-test/qnx-safety-monitor/qnx-safety-monitor-unmask
# The SDV direction's guest monitors (kind 4 VSS claims; the Autoware plan's control and gap
# kinds), named before the first build, for the same reasons.
ipc-test/qnx-safety-monitor/qnx-safety-monitor-vss
ipc-test/qnx-safety-monitor/qnx-safety-monitor-carla
ipc-test/qnx-safety-monitor/qnx-safety-monitor-ctl
ipc-test/qnx-safety-monitor/qnx-safety-monitor-gap

# Secrets / credentials / cloud
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
# Device certificates (AWS IoT hands out *.pem.crt) and key stores
*.crt
*.p12
*.pfx
# The twin's device directory keeps its endpoint and names in this file (sdv/stack: --env-file). The stack
# refuses a device directory inside the repo; this is for a copy made by hand.
connector.env
.ec2-instance-id
.ec2-*.json
.aws/

# Build artifacts
# ipc-test extensionless QNX binaries (NCEULA: never commit compiled QNX code).
ipc-test/qnx-server/qnx-echo-server
ipc-test/qnx-host-client/qnx-host-client
ipc-test/qnx-server-net/qnx-echo-server-net
ipc-test/qnx-server-net/qnx-echo-server-sweep
ipc-test/qnx-server-net/qnx-echo-server-reads
ipc-test/qnx-server-net/qnx-echo-server-timed
ipc-test/qnx-server-net/qnx-echo-server-spin
ipc-test/qnx-ipcbench/qnx-ipcbench
ipc-test/qnx-safety-monitor/qnx-safety-monitor
ipc-test/qnx-dds-monitor/qnx-dds-monitor
ipc-test/qnx-clockctl/qnx-clockctl
ipc-test/qnx-tracectl/qnx-tracectl
ipc-test/qnx-someip/qnx-someip-monitor
ipc-test/qnx-its-probe/qnx-its-probe
ipc-test/qnx-its-probe/qnx-its-probe-2v

# Interview / application material: local only, never published (owner,
# 2026-09-20 for the narrative, 2026-09-21 for the JD mapping).
#
# This hides the file from the tip only. The owner reviewed its earlier
# publication and chose to keep the history; do not re-raise that decision.
# Rewriting it would break the commit references in the public documentation.
docs/interview-narrative.md
# Same rule, same reason: architecture brief written for CV prep (2026-09-20).
# This one has never been committed, so it leaves no history behind it.
docs/cv-architecture-brief.md
# Same rule, same reason: a table mapping a job description to repo artefacts.
# Untracked from the tip on 2026-09-21; history is kept -- see the note above.
# Its basename is also in
# claims_lib.LOCAL_ONLY so the prose scan skips it locally as CI does.
docs/jd-mapping.md
# Phase-0 session-resume prompt: unpublished development instructions.
# Current public state and the honest-framing rule belong in README.
docs/onboarding-prompt.md
# idlc-generated sources: regenerated at build time from av.idl, and they carry
# no licence header of their own, so they are not committed.
ipc-test/qnx-dds-monitor/av.c
ipc-test/qnx-dds-monitor/av.h
ipc-test/qnx-host-shmem-probe/hyp-shm-probe
ipc-test/qnx-host-shmem-probe/hyp-shm-roundtrip
ipc-test/qnx-guest-shmem-probe/gshm-probe
# ipc-test extensionless Linux binary (ordinary build artifact, not QNX-derived,
# but still a compiled binary with no reason to be committed).
ipc-test/linux-client/linux-client
*.o
*.a
*.so
*.dylib
*.dll
*.elf
*.efi
*.dtb
*.itb
build/
out/
artifacts/

# Phase 3b board-run record directories: evaluation output under NC QDL v7 4.6(i).
# The curated records and designs live directly under results/orin-native-port/<utc>/,
# never in these per-milestone subdirectories.
results/orin-native-port/*/m3/
results/orin-native-port/*/m4/
results/orin-native-port/*/m5/
results/orin-native-port/*/s1/

# Logs (allow only the curated samples under logs/sample-boot/)
*.log
!logs/sample-boot/*.log
# Curated run records under results/orin-native-port/<utc>/ are evidence, not
# build noise -- the .out files in those directories are already tracked, and a
# blanket *.log silently excluded the guest-side captures that findings.md cites
# (2026-09-18: both the KVM-concurrency and cross-partition-demo consoles).
!results/orin-native-port/*/*.log
# 2026-09-21: the A6 campaign records keep their raw traces one and two levels
# deeper (<exp>/raw/, dry-run-stalls/<run>/), and the rule above stops at one
# level, so the placement and clock traces the records cite went untracked.
# Deliberately NARROW: a first try with results/orin-native-port/**/*.log also
# exposed M4 dry-run and TCG logs, which stay local under 4.6(i).
!results/orin-native-port/*T-a6-*/*/*.log
!results/orin-native-port/*T-a6-*/*/raw/*.log
!results/orin-native-port/*T-a6-*/dry-run-stalls/*/*.log
# The shift isolation keeps one directory per boot (session*/b<i>-<cond>/, and
# kvm0|kvm1 inside it); its console and ladder logs are part of the record.
!results/orin-native-port/*T-a6-*/session*/b*/*.log
!results/orin-native-port/*T-a6-*/session*/b*/kvm*/*.log
# The LLM prep record keeps the windows it discarded under exploratory/, one
# level deeper; the OOM logs there are the evidence for its page-cache finding.
!results/orin-native-port/*T-a6-*/exploratory/*/*.log

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.venv/
venv/

# Editor / OS noise
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*.swo
*.code-workspace

# Claude Code: per-user local settings stay out; project-shared subagents go in.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/.credentials.json

# Phase 3b (native Orin port) build outputs. The shim source is committed; the
# assembled page and any image concatenated with a QNX IFS are not — the latter
# would carry QNX bytes (NCEULA).
orin-native/shim/out/
orin-native/startup/**/*.o
orin-native/startup/**/*.dep
orin-native/**/startup-t234-orin-nano
*.kimg
# the user-space tools are source here; the built binaries are outputs
orin-native/tools/tcu-cat
orin-native/tools/stamp
orin-native/tools/smpcheck
orin-native/tools/bwait
orin-native/tools/clkcmp
orin-native/tools/trcctl
orin-native/tools/m4count
orin-native/tools/s1con
orin-native/tools/memcanary
orin-native/tools/memcanary-w

# mkifs [+keeplinked] drops symbol files next to the buildfile; they are derived
# from QNX binaries and must never be committed.
*.sym

# The agent roster is local development tooling. The public repository does
# not assert a team structure from these definitions. Both trees stay local.
agents/
.claude/agents/

# AI briefings are private development tooling. README is the one public
# statement of current state. Both files remain available to the local tools.
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md

# AI tooling config and AI-written study notes: private, kept on the build
# machine. Removed from the public repo 2026-09-21 with agents/ and CLAUDE.md.
.codex/
skills/

# 2026-09-27 (owner): measurement results stay local (NC QDL v7 4.6(i)). These are
# the paths the tooling writes evaluation output to; they are ignored so nothing a
# run produces reaches the public tree by accident. Records go to the unpushed
# branches only, with `git add -f` there.
results/cloud/*-latest.csv
results/hw/*-latest.csv
results/gicv3-nisv-debug/
results/orin-native-port/[0-9]*T-*/
logs/sample-boot/*.log
logs/sample-boot/*.txt

# The SDV direction's generated and runtime output inside the tree: VSS-generated artefacts,
# databroker/feeder/connector output, the local manifest and spool, Ditto and hawkBit data,
# certificates. One ignored root; recordings live outside the repo (~/sdv-recordings/).
sdv-out/
